  <!--
    WorkflowStage : WorkflowStageType

    WorkflowStageType                            | WorkflowStage Usage
    .............................................|........................................................
        @pending: platform:IndicatorType  [0..1] | whether stage change is pending appoval or preparation
        Code    : WorkflowStageCodeType   [0..1] | processing stage for workflow such as Started
        DateTime: DateTimeType            [0..1] | when this stage was entered
        Note    : platform:NoteType       [0..*] | note about change to this stage
  -->
  <xs:element name="WorkflowStage" type="WorkflowStageType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>A workflow stage annotated with a timestamp and notes</xs:documentation>
      <xs:documentation>The intent is for multiple stage values to represent a progression in time for the workflow.  The DateTime field provides the natural ordering and is recommended over the the sequential ordering of &lt;Stage&gt; fields.  However, agcXML does not mandate how to order stages.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:complexType name="WorkflowStageType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>A workflow stage annotated with a timestamp and notes</xs:documentation>
      <xs:documentation>The intent is for multiple stage values to represent a progression in time for the workflow.  The DateTime field provides the natural ordering and is recommended over the the sequential ordering of &lt;Stage&gt; fields.  However, agcXML does not mandate how to order stages.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="Code" type="WorkflowStageCodeType" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Current stage of a work item such as composing a response to an RFI line item.</xs:documentation>
          <xs:documentation>Enumerated values are:  Suggested, NotStarted, Started, Paused, Canceled, Error, Complete.  This is an open code list in agcXML.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element ref="DateTime" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>When this stage was entered</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="Note" type="platform:NoteType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>A note about the workflow's entry to this stage or at any point while in this stage.  Notes here are reserved for the stage itself such as an explicit acknowledgement by a participant or a reason why a Canceled stage was entered.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
    <xs:attribute name="pending" type="platform:IndicatorType">
      <xs:annotation>
        <xs:documentation>When this indicator is true, the change to the stage value in field Code is in progress.</xs:documentation>
        <xs:documentation>For example, an approval might be required or final information collected from other parties before changing the stage.</xs:documentation>
        <xs:documentation>Approvals can take real time during which different parties see the workflow stage a little differently.  The approving party still considers the work in progress whereas the submitting party considers it done except for the approval.  This fine distinction during a transitional time can be represented with this indicator.</xs:documentation>
      </xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>
</xs:schema>